[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3235266241","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3235266241","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3235266241,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A1j7B","user":{"login":"conde2","id":2137569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzc1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2137569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2","html_url":"https://github.com/conde2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-28T23:38:32Z","updated_at":"2025-08-28T23:38:32Z","body":"Setting it to Edgecenter is even worse, almost all paths are crazy like that:\n<img width=\"526\" height=\"40\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dedc8eef-896a-40b5-8a4d-14e648868cb5\" />\n<img width=\"707\" height=\"337\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/46ded308-0b59-4d0c-9cb5-1318025425f2\" />\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3235266241/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3235954884","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3235954884","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3235954884,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A4MDE","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T07:00:12Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T07:00:12Z","body":"If you have any navmesh merge errors reported you need to fix them as wrong or not merged navmesh edges will create all kinds of pathing bugs.\n\nIf there are no reported error it is due to the created navmesh layout with long and very thin edges. Astar travels from polygon to polygon to build the path corridor. It moves from closest edge point to closest edge point. So if the edges are very long and thin and nearly overlapping it will commonly end up having polygon corridors that lead to huge detours.\n\nTry using squares or hexagon shapes instead of circles which are some of the worst shapes to use for navmesh baking. Each single circle edge forces the creation of a navmesh edge. So when you use circle shapes for every single prop in your level you end up with thousands of almost useless little navmesh edges that create a very low quality navmesh when baked.\n\nThe `path_max_distance` property has nothing to do with any of that. It is the maximum distance the agent is allowed away from the path when following the path points. If the agent goes over this distance to the current path segment it queries a new path.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3235954884/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237016506","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3237016506","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3237016506,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A8PO6","user":{"login":"conde2","id":2137569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzc1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2137569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2","html_url":"https://github.com/conde2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T13:18:17Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T13:18:17Z","body":"@smix8  The only error I'm getting when baking is this spam:\n\n```\nERROR: No TileSet atlas source with id 2.\n```\n\nBut I don't think this is related, I really don't have source with id 2, and I don't know why it complains.\nThis is how my navmesh looks like and how it is configured:\n\n<img width=\"1349\" height=\"778\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa98b184-16df-4e11-84b0-cbdeb859213e\" />\n\nTried with square shapes it is better, but I'm getting now infinite paths, it can never finish the path.\nMy tilemaplayer navigation layer is disable, because I'm baking into a NavigationRegion2D\n\n<img width=\"556\" height=\"466\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b782262b-aa18-4549-b0c7-ef0addfaadd2\" />\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4f12590-7332-4760-954b-6e0af40715eb","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237016506/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237023515","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3237023515","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3237023515,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A8Q8b","user":{"login":"conde2","id":2137569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzc1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2137569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2","html_url":"https://github.com/conde2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T13:20:43Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T13:20:43Z","body":"Using squares is better but still gives me this weird paths:\n\n<img width=\"1090\" height=\"453\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/023941dc-ca57-436b-b210-a1c5d01433f0\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237023515/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237024516","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3237024516","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3237024516,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A8RME","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T13:21:05Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T13:21:05Z","body":"I'd suggest trying to fix that issue first as it might affect the navigation, or at least to make sure you can see error messages properly\n\nBut in any case this needs an MRP to be able to test properly","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237024516/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237054899","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3237054899","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3237054899,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A8Ymz","user":{"login":"conde2","id":2137569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzc1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2137569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2","html_url":"https://github.com/conde2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T13:31:46Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T13:31:46Z","body":"> I'd suggest trying to fix that issue first as it might affect the navigation, or at least to make sure you can see error messages properly\n> \n> But in any case this needs an MRP to be able to test properly\n\nI fixed the TileMapLayer errors. I had forgotten to delete some tiles after removing the TileSet atlas source.\n\nUnfortunately, that didn’t resolve the issue, so we’re still facing the navigation problem.\n\nI’m currently investigating the cause and will try to create a reproducible project later if necessary. However, I’d prefer to investigate further first, since it might just turn out to be a simple misconfiguration.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237054899/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237059629","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3237059629","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3237059629,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A8Zwt","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T13:33:27Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T13:33:27Z","body":"> The only error I'm getting when baking is this spam:\n\nThe error will only print once per project start. So if you already missed it you will need to restart the project. It is print-once because on a typical TileMap with messed up layout it would spam a few thousand error msgs causing the editor to lag and burn.\n\n> My tilemaplayer navigation layer is disable, because I'm baking into a NavigationRegion2D\n\nIn that image all that it shows is that the `navigation_layers` bitmask is set to zero. The navigation_layers are path query filters for regions. They do nothing at all for the navmesh layout. You need to actually disable the boolean on/off of the TileMap build-in navigation if you want to turn it off, else it will conflict with whatever navmesh you add on top of it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237059629/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237087774","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3237087774","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3237087774,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A8goe","user":{"login":"conde2","id":2137569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzc1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2137569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2","html_url":"https://github.com/conde2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T13:41:09Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T14:17:00Z","body":"> > The only error I'm getting when baking is this spam:\n> \n> The error will only print once per project start. So if you already missed it you will need to restart the project. It is print-once because on a typical TileMap with messed up layout it would spam a few thousand error msgs causing the editor to lag and burn.\n> \n> > My tilemaplayer navigation layer is disable, because I'm baking into a NavigationRegion2D\n> \n> In that image all that it shows is that the `navigation_layers` bitmask is set to zero. The navigation_layers are path query filters for regions. They do nothing at all for the navmesh layout. You need to actually disable the boolean on/off of the TileMap build-in navigation if you want to turn it off, else it will conflict with whatever navmesh you add on top of it.\n\nMy agent was querying in layer 1, so I thought it would be enough to simply remove that layer. After baking, I deleted the NavigationLayer from my TileMapLayer, and that fixed the issue of the agent moving cycling paths unnecessarily.\n\nI can’t disable the TileMapLayer entirely since it contains my ground tiles, but I might delete the NavigationLayer in the _ready() function at runtime instead.\n\nNow, the only remaining issue is the strange pathing behavior.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237087774/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237170182","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3237170182","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3237170182,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A80wG","user":{"login":"conde2","id":2137569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzc1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2137569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2","html_url":"https://github.com/conde2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T14:09:54Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T14:10:13Z","body":"@smix8 after some digging I found that the issue is with the path postprocessing.\n\nWhen setting to Corridorfunel it gives me this weird paths with polygon corridors. Even worse when using the Edgecentered (almost always stuck in polygon corridors)\n\nSo the solution was setting to NONE, and it fixed most of the issues so far.\n\n<img width=\"539\" height=\"142\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e074fa08-7f03-4656-913c-e2a1fc2dc1c1\" />\n\n\nCorridorfunel \n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/543c2d98-50cb-40f1-bc99-97cfcd175d83\n\nEdgecentered\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e40ba1db-3505-4759-9044-147153ee32a1\n\nNone\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2535add3-ca2d-478d-a73d-2804b4fb225f","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237170182/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237240515","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3237240515","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3237240515,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A9F7D","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T14:31:40Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T14:35:01Z","body":"> I can’t disable the TileMapLayer entirely since it contains my ground tiles, but I might delete the NavigationLayer in the _ready() function at runtime instead.\n\nYou do not need to delete the entire NavigationLayer from the TileMap. There is a setting on the TileMap to just disable it, so the data is still there but the TileMap does not spawn its own build-in navmesh at runtime.\n\n> When setting to Corridorfunel it gives me this weird paths with polygon corridors. Even worse when using the Edgecentered (almost always stuck in polygon corridors)\n\nThat is the result of those long and thin edges. In the video alone I can already see tiny mini edges that nearly overlap and since the corridorfunnel snaps to corridor edges, having a bad path corridor caused by such a layout causes even worse path result with the corridorfunnel postprocessing.\n\nMeanwhile the NONE postprocessing option uses the raw path corridor from astar as a debug. That traveled from closest edge point to closest edge point. Not very optimal as far as a path is concerned but since corridorfunnel has to work with a low quality corridor the debug path looks more reasonable in this case.\n\nI rather would fix the layout by avoiding those long mini edges because the debug path is not a good way to path travel. E.g. use a chunk grid with multiple navigation regions to bake to break up all those long edges. You can find a demo project for that here https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/2d/navigation_mesh_chunks","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237240515/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237259916","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3237259916","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3237259916,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A9KqM","user":{"login":"conde2","id":2137569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzc1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2137569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2","html_url":"https://github.com/conde2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T14:37:47Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T14:38:42Z","body":"I’ll go ahead and close this since it’s not a bug but rather due to how my navmesh is set up. Thank you for your patience and for all the explanations. I also really appreciate you sharing the Navigation Mesh Chunks project that I can use as a reference. Truly, thank you.\n\nIs there any proposal do make this built in the engien itself?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237259916/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237265053","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110071#issuecomment-3237265053","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110071","id":3237265053,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A9L6d","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T14:39:32Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T14:39:32Z","body":"> Is there any proposal do make this built in the engien itself?\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12707\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12665","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237265053/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]